WEBVTT

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.782
AG: Think about how crystallized
intelligence comes in handy in your job.

00:07:02.806 --> 00:07:03.982
If you're in sales,

00:07:04.006 --> 00:07:06.752
you've used it to tailor your pitches
to different clients

00:07:06.776 --> 00:07:09.276
based on what you've learned
about them in the past.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.506
If you're in government,

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.532
you've relied on it
to get around red tape.

00:07:12.556 --> 00:07:14.723
If you're in finance,
maybe you've applied it

00:07:14.747 --> 00:07:17.053
to predict how markets
are affected by crises.

00:07:17.077 --> 00:07:20.907
Crystallized intelligence peaks
much later than fluid intelligence,

00:07:20.931 --> 00:07:23.762
in large part because our body
of knowledge keeps growing.

00:07:23.786 --> 00:07:25.932
AB: Think of it like a library.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:31.213
Think of the brain as basically
filling up with a lot of volumes.